        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The single most important property for what follows is that (2) is a second-moment objective: every quantity in the estimator derives from cross-covariances alone. When the data within a node are homogeneous – a single local linear law with Gaussian scatter – the covariance criterion is the right one. When the node instead contains a mixture of regimes, the criterion is no longer sufficient. For that reason, a criterion based on third co-moments is adopted in what follows.",
            "block_bbox": [
