        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Write  $ t = Xw $ and  $ u = Yv $ for a generic pair of score vectors. Beside the covariance  $ \\mathbb{E}[t u] $ that drives (2), the two third-order cross-moments of the pair are  $ \\mathbb{E}[t^2 u] $ and  $ \\mathbb{E}[t u^2] $. The coskewness decomposition retains the architecture of Section 2: two deflation loops, each pairing its own deflated block with the other block in full. However, the second order",
